letters.body:
Dear Commissioners,

I am the attorney for {{client}} (DOB {{dob}}) and I am writing regarding his entitlement to aftercare services under section 117 of the Mental Health Act 1983.

{{detentionParagraph}}

Section 117 imposes a joint duty on the local authority and the Integrated Care Board to provide aftercare services — including, where assessed as needed, residential placement — to persons who have been detained under s3. The duty:

• is a statutory entitlement that neither expires with the detention nor depends on waiting lists;
• is not discharged by workforce shortages, and does not queue behind the current 8-week social-worker allocation gap;
• can lawfully fund and mandate the fully managed 24-hour residential placement his documented risk profile requires.

I therefore ask the joint commissioners to:

1. Confirm the detention history and the s117 entitlement within 7 days (by {{clockDate}}).
2. Convene a joint s117 care-planning meeting within 14 days.
3. Confirm funding responsibility for the placement pending that meeting.

The evidence pack (coverage analysis, medication failures, elopement record and call chronology) accompanies the Best Interests statement.

Yours faithfully,
{{attorney}}
Attorney under registered LPA — {{today}}
